Cmn1=You must pair with the Apple TV before this module will work. First||1
Cmn2=start the\\pairing process by pulsing StartPairing, then using the||1
Cmn3=Apple TV remote\\navigate to: Settings > Remotes and Devices > Remote||1
Cmn4=App and Devices,\\ select Crestron under Pairable Devices.\\Use||1
Cmn5=0 0 0 0 as the password. That’s it, you can now use the module.\\
Cmn6=\\The wake up process does not work over wireless. So if you need||1
Cmn7=to\\use wireless, set sleep mode to never.\\\\\\Up, Down, Left,||1
Cmn8=Right, Select, Menu & PlayPause work just like the remote.\\\\InUse||1
Cmn9=– Will wake up the Apple TV then send the release command every||1
Cmn10=\\15min to keep the Apple TV awake.  If you have your Apple TV set||1
Cmn11=to never\\sleep this is not needed. Keep it high as long as the||1
Cmn12=Apple TV is needed.\\\\StartPairing – Starts the IOS pairing process.
Cmn13=\\\\CancelPairing – Cancels the pairing process.\\\\StartPairing_FB||1
Cmn14=– This will go high and remain high until Pairing is complete.\\
Cmn15=\\{{**{{NeedsPairing}}**}} – This will go high if you try to send a command||1
Cmn16=and the \\Apple TV replies with not paired.\\\\Apple TV’s IP Address||1
Cmn17=– this is the IP Address of the Apple TV.  You will want to\\set||1
Cmn18=this as static and/or use a dhcp reservation.  If this address changes,||1
Cmn19=control\\will stop working.\\\\Apple TV’s Mac Address – You can||1
Cmn20=find this under Settings > General > About\\it is labeled Ethernet||1
Cmn21=Address.  This is used by the InUse command.\\\\Crestron’s IP Address||1
Cmn22=– The IP Address of the Crestron processor that\\will control the||1
Cmn23=Apple TV.
